S4.5  "photoreal nail" predicate (accept/amend/replace):
AMEND.

A material class passes only when:

1. The renderer contains genuine independent material components, including:

   * base/body colour
   * curvature-dependent shading
   * broad specular response
   * sharper highlight response
   * edge/rim response
   * cuticle/root integration
   * appropriate texture/noise where material demands it

2. Highlight and shading move/respond coherently to the nail geometry rather than being static decorative overlays.

3. Objective image measurements show plausible apex/edge luminance falloff and material contrast relative to the reference class.

4. Edges remain clean at intended output resolution:

   * no obvious clipping
   * no staircase aliasing
   * no flat SVG/sticker appearance

5. It is evaluated across multiple nail shapes and colours, not a single cherry-picked design.

6. Vision review should target ≥8/10 on material realism, but this score is advisory because S4.2 makes vision non-binding.

7. Binding subjective acceptance is one explicit human sign-off per material class:

   * glossy
   * matte
   * metallic/chrome
   * glitter
   * translucent/jelly
   * relevant textured/special finishes

Once a material class is approved, its golden fixtures become regression-protected.

S4.6  "AR doesn't float" predicate (accept/amend/replace):
AMEND and strengthen.

On a fixed recorded hand fixture plus eventual physical-device validation:

1. Nail position remains anchored to its corresponding physical nail landmark.

2. Scale changes correctly as the finger moves toward/away from camera.

3. Nail orientation follows finger orientation.

4. Perspective/foreshortening visibly responds when the finger rotates >30° from camera-facing.

5. Nail/root alignment remains attached at the cuticle instead of pivoting around the centre.

6. A plausible contact/ambient shadow is rendered separately from the nail layer.

7. Finger/hand segmentation correctly occludes the synthetic nail where geometry requires it.

8. Occlusion should hide ≥90% of pixels that should be behind the hand/finger in the away-facing fixture cases.

9. Static-hold positional jitter target: <2 px RMS in the canonical recorded fixture after stabilisation.

10. No obvious scale pumping, one-frame teleporting, incorrect finger assignment or orientation inversion.

11. Human side-by-side video sign-off is required for final acceptance.

S4.7  motion-quality predicate (accept/amend):
ACCEPT with wording clarification.

* scripted interaction frame-time p95 ≤16.7ms on the canonical performance target;
* continuous animation/gesture work must not depend on JS-thread frame-by-frame execution where Reanimated/UI-thread execution is appropriate;
* every intentional transition appears in a motion manifest;
* durations/easing/springs reference named motion tokens;
* reduced-motion behaviour exists;
* interruption/reversal of gestures must not leave components in invalid intermediate states.

S4.8  performance budgets (accept mine or give numbers):
Use:

* cold start to first meaningful paint: <2.0s on canonical test hardware
* normal UI/scroll p95 frame time: ≤16.7ms
* editor direct-manipulation response: <50ms
* normal editor target: 60fps
* AR: sustained ≥30fps on canonical device; brief dips may occur but not sustained sub-24fps operation
* JS/application bundle target: <25 MB excluding fonts and intentionally curated catalogue media
* track catalogue/media separately rather than cheating the figure
* initial installed product should aim to remain under ~80 MB unless evidence justifies exceeding it
* editor memory: <350 MB
* no unbounded memory growth during a 10-minute scripted editor session

